{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.BraneGeometricResummation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BraneGeometricResummation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.brane_resum_mul_one_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.brane_resum_mul_one_sub","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BraneGeometricResummation.lean#L48-L53","doc":"The fixed-point relation in product form: `S = a + r·S → S·(1 − r) = a`. Combined with\n`r ≠ 1` this is the closed form `S = a/(1−r)` (the final division needs a field tactic\noutside the cache). Proof avoids `ring` by treating `r·S` linearly via `mul_one_sub`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.brane_resum_affine_fixed_point","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.brane_resum_affine_fixed_point","kind":"theorem","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BraneGeometricResummation.lean#L39-L46","doc":"**Brane resummation is an affine fixed point (eq ★, verifiable core).** The resummed\nℏ²-damped brane tower value `S` satisfies the self-consistency `S = a + r·S` (level-1 term\n`a := ℏ_q²·tower^{(1)}` plus the damped-lifted remainder `r·S`, `r := ℏ_q²z²`) **iff**\n`S − r·S = a`. The latter gives `S·(1 − r) = a`, hence the closed form `S = a/(1−r)` for\n`r ≠ 1` (the division step needs `field_simp`, outside the sandbox cache — see module doc). ","signatureChunk":0}]}